@prefix backlog: <http://example.org/backlog#> .
@prefix ex:      <http://example.org/sen0414-ch1011simp-lineage#> .
@prefix owl:     <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

<http://example.org/sen0414-ch1011simp-lineage> a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "Urgent narrow lineage: SEN0414 chapters 10 and 11, one code, one environment"@en ;
    owl:versionInfo "1.45.0" ; owl:versionIRI <http://example.org/sen0414-ch1011simp-lineage/1.45.0> ; dcterms:identifier "sen0414_ch1011simp_lineage" ;
    rdfs:comment """1.45.0 (2026-11-25): Scope change only (one stage per version). The Owner's ruling of 2026-11-24 that everyday analogies are misleading and must not appear anywhere in course materials is applied to chapters 10 and 11. Discipline files re-read from GitHub on 2026-11-25 (OE 2.41.0, lineage discipline 163.0.7 are the latest)."""@en .

ex:CR11_NoAnalogies a backlog:ChangeRequest ;
    rdfs:label "Remove everyday analogies from chapters 10 and 11 and put plain literal explanations in their place"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo ex:Scope11 ; backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "Owner's ruling of 2026-11-24 (content, not a verbatim quotation): there are to be no everyday analogies anywhere in the course materials (decks, pages, chapter code, generators), because they mislead. The Owner's reply of 2026-11-25, OK, proceed, to my statement that this change comes next. The slide count must not change." ;
    backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted .
ex:IA11_NoAnalogies a backlog:ImpactAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Where the analogies are today, measured before planning"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest ex:CR11_NoAnalogies ; backlog:identifiesAffectedLineage ex:Lineage11 ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "MEASURED FACTS (2026-11-25, read-only): chapter 10 deck has 7 analogy slides titled Everyday pictures, holding 52 concept lines, and chapter 11 deck has 5 such slides with 23 concept lines; each deck also carries two fixed analogy sentences (a packing list for the summary, finger scales for the practice slide) that the shared deck builder of other chapters carries too. The lecture tab of the chapter 11 page repeats the five slides' text; the speaker notes of the analogy slides use the same pictures (notes 4.0.0: 4 phrase hits in chapter 10, 2 in chapter 11; the later notes files have none in these phrases); chapter 10's code source has 1 phrase hit that grooming must read. Replacing the content on the same slides keeps the slide count at 41 in both decks. The two decks' page tests, deck checks and the code check must be re-run, and the previous versions stay. Other chapters carry the same builder sentences and the same kind of slides; they are out of this lineage." ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Excluded and stated: chapters 1 to 9 and 12 to 25. Decision made by me, not asked: the analogy slides become plain slides that say what each concept does in a program, in literal words, with no comparison to another thing." .
ex:Area11_NoAnalogies a backlog:ScopeArea ; rdfs:label "No everyday analogies in chapters 10 and 11"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage11 .
ex:Del11_NoAnalogies a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ; rdfs:label "Chapters 10 and 11 decks and pages without everyday analogies, slide count unchanged"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage11 ; backlog:deliverableForArea ex:Area11_NoAnalogies .
ex:SC11_NoAnalogies a backlog:ScopeChange ;
    rdfs:label "Scope grown by removing everyday analogies from chapters 10 and 11"@en ;
    backlog:fulfillsRequest ex:CR11_NoAnalogies ; backlog:changesScope ex:Scope11 ; backlog:decidedBy backlog:Owner ;
    backlog:admitsItem ex:Area11_NoAnalogies, ex:Del11_NoAnalogies ;
    backlog:hasScopeChangeRationale "Owner's ruling of 2026-11-24 and go-ahead of 2026-11-25. One area and one deliverable added; other chapters stay excluded." .
ex:Scope11 backlog:coversArea ex:Area11_NoAnalogies ; backlog:hasScopeDeliverable ex:Del11_NoAnalogies .
